WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.770
Hi! Can an ordinary iron nail become a magnet? Today we'll learn two ways to make magnets, and see what magnets are used for.

2
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:18.258
The stroke method: rub one pole of a magnet along the iron nail, in the same direction, many times.

3
00:00:18.408 --> 00:00:24.498
The nail becomes a magnet and can pick up paper clips, but it won't stay magnetic for ever.

4
00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:35.874
The electrical method: coil wire round an iron nail many times and connect a battery. When current flows, the nail becomes magnetic. This is an electromagnet.

5
00:00:36.024 --> 00:00:42.210
When the current is switched off, the electromagnet loses its magnetism.

6
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:49.074
More coils of wire, or more batteries, make a stronger electromagnet that picks up more paper clips.

7
00:00:49.224 --> 00:00:54.210
Fridge magnets and magnetic door catches use magnets to hold things.

8
00:00:54.360 --> 00:01:00.330
The magnetic needle in a compass points north and south, which helps people find their way.

9
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:08.226
In a scrapyard, an electromagnet crane picks up scrap iron and drops it when the current is switched off.

10
00:01:08.376 --> 00:01:16.482
Watch out! Some pupils rub the magnet back and forth on the nail. That way the nail hardly becomes a magnet!

11
00:01:16.632 --> 00:01:24.138
Use the same pole and always rub in the same direction. At the end, lift the magnet up and go back to the start.

12
00:01:24.288 --> 00:01:29.922
The more times you stroke it, the stronger the nail's magnetism.

13
00:01:30.072 --> 00:01:39.762
Your turn! What happens when an electromagnet's current is switched off? Pause and think.

14
00:01:39.912 --> 00:01:45.306
It loses its magnetism. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:45.456 --> 00:01:54.306
Another one! How can we make an electromagnet stronger? Pause and think.

16
00:01:54.456 --> 00:02:00.618
Add more coils of wire, or more batteries. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:00.768 --> 00:02:11.250
Here's another! Can we use the stroke method to turn an aluminium strip into a magnet? Pause and think.

18
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:21.666
No. Aluminium isn't magnetic. Only materials like iron and steel can be magnetised. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:21.816 --> 00:02:30.786
Try one more! What does the magnetic needle in a compass do? Pause and think.

20
00:02:30.936 --> 00:02:37.602
It points north and south, helping us find our way. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:37.752 --> 00:02:48.378
Last one! Why do scrapyards use electromagnet cranes, not ordinary magnets? Pause and think.

22
00:02:48.528 --> 00:02:56.418
An electromagnet can be switched on to lift scrap iron and off to drop it. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:56.568 --> 00:03:08.706
Remember: in the stroke method, use one pole and one direction many times. An electromagnet is magnetic only when current flows, and more coils or batteries make it stronger.

24
00:03:08.856 --> 00:03:13.146
Find things at home that use magnets!

